WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.198 --> 00:00:02.809
- Good morning believe nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael,

00:00:02.809 --> 00:00:04.241
my one word is believe

00:00:04.241 --> 00:00:06.690
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.316
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:10.462
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:13.763
today's message is create
something different.

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:15.903
Over to you Shigeru Miyamoto.

00:00:15.903 --> 00:00:18.259
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.259 --> 00:00:20.930
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.120
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.287
♫ I wake up every morning ♫

00:01:18.318 --> 00:01:20.262
So as entrepreneurs, we like
to create different things.

00:01:20.262 --> 00:01:21.792
It's part of what we do.

00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:23.250
We don't like working for the may,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.832
we don't want a typical corporate job,

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:26.370
we want to create our own thing.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.785
We want to self express

00:01:27.785 --> 00:01:29.800
and we want to make something different.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.881
I think that's something
that should speak to you

00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:33.590
as an entrepreneur if you're
watching this channel.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.505
I feel like I'm already
speaking to the converted

00:01:35.505 --> 00:01:37.764
and I don't need to express the importance

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.233
of making something different.

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:41.808
That's what we do as
entrepreneurs, that's our role.

00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:43.468
Here's a challenge that I think that

00:01:43.468 --> 00:01:45.457
makes it difficult for entrepreneurs.

00:01:45.457 --> 00:01:49.762
We don't continue enough
to make different things.

00:01:49.762 --> 00:01:52.199
Entrepreneurs are really good at the start

00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:54.308
of coming up with some bold brand new idea

00:01:54.308 --> 00:01:56.804
and then launching it.

00:01:56.804 --> 00:01:58.487
Now whether it becomes successful or not,

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:00.722
tweaking, tweaking, tweaking,
trial and error, testing,

00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:03.182
customer feedback 'til you hit something.

00:02:03.182 --> 00:02:05.193
What ends up happening next though

00:02:05.193 --> 00:02:07.173
is what screws over a
lot of entrepreneurs,

00:02:07.173 --> 00:02:10.854
they stop creating something different.

00:02:10.854 --> 00:02:12.986
Because they found this thing

00:02:12.986 --> 00:02:14.823
that they think is a recipe for success,

00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:17.921
they found the one way to do
something that was different

00:02:17.921 --> 00:02:20.197
and they're doing it over
and over and over again

00:02:20.197 --> 00:02:21.960
and it's generating cash for them

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.516
then they stop evolving.

00:02:23.516 --> 00:02:26.616
And that's the death
toll for an entrepreneur.

00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:29.764
If you are not continuing to evolve,

00:02:29.764 --> 00:02:32.199
to create new things, to be different,

00:02:32.199 --> 00:02:34.716
then you're going to get
bored of your business

00:02:34.716 --> 00:02:36.553
and this happens to so many entrepreneurs.

00:02:36.553 --> 00:02:38.270
I can't tell you how many
entrepreneurs I talked to

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.941
that are three, four, five
years into the company and say,

00:02:40.941 --> 00:02:43.590
"I'm bored, I'm looking
for something different.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.008
"I don't know, maybe
I'll sell my business."

00:02:46.008 --> 00:02:48.877
Or they start on some
like passion project,

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:51.461
some side thing that they
want to get going and doing.

00:02:51.461 --> 00:02:53.204
And here's what happened.

00:02:53.204 --> 00:02:56.264
They had so much creative
energy, and so much difference

00:02:56.264 --> 00:02:58.760
going into the first part of
their business in the beginning

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.716
and then they found the thing that worked

00:03:00.716 --> 00:03:03.236
and so they stuck with that
and they stop evolving.

00:03:03.236 --> 00:03:04.760
They evolved as a human.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.697
We constantly evolve, we
constantly get new interests,

00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:08.786
we constantly want to try new things.

00:03:08.786 --> 00:03:09.966
They evolved and grew,

00:03:09.966 --> 00:03:12.024
but they didn't grow
their business with them.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:15.376
Your business should
constantly be a reflection

00:03:15.376 --> 00:03:18.471
of who you are and what
you're interested in doing.

00:03:18.471 --> 00:03:20.816
If you are sticking down a business line

00:03:20.816 --> 00:03:23.385
that you are not passionate about anymore,

00:03:23.385 --> 00:03:25.160
then you're never going
to have huge success.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.973
If that's you, if you are not passionate

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.153
all about your business,

00:03:28.153 --> 00:03:31.322
then chances are, you grew too
far away from your business.

00:03:31.322 --> 00:03:33.675
You grew and your business stayed here.

00:03:33.675 --> 00:03:35.494
And even though it's making money,

00:03:35.494 --> 00:03:37.530
it's not interesting to you anymore.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.492
And so if that's you, sell it
and go find something else.

00:03:41.492 --> 00:03:43.790
Don't find some side hobby passion thing.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.618
Get out of your entire business
and go try something else.

00:03:46.618 --> 00:03:48.561
And for the next one,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.011
and if you guys aren't at that
point yet in your business,

00:03:51.011 --> 00:03:52.472
where you get bored of it

00:03:52.472 --> 00:03:53.500
or you're just on the cusp,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.966
evolve your company with you.

00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:59.104
So if you look at my
business, it started off

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:00.514
me doing seminars.

00:04:00.514 --> 00:04:02.720
I was invited to speak, I sold my company

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.049
when I was 22 years old, how old am I now?

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:06.979
37.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:08.901
So it's 15 years doing this.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.294
It's easy to get bored.

00:04:10.294 --> 00:04:11.948
Now I still love helping entrepreneurs.

00:04:11.948 --> 00:04:13.702
That is still a huge passion of mine.

00:04:13.702 --> 00:04:15.879
But the execution of it changes.

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:18.692
It started off me just doing
speaking, and I love that.

00:04:18.692 --> 00:04:21.748
And then it evolved to
me doing my website,

00:04:21.748 --> 00:04:23.706
and I love that.

00:04:23.706 --> 00:04:25.653
And that evolved from me
focusing on my website

00:04:25.653 --> 00:04:28.679
to spending a lot more time
on Youtube, and I love this.

00:04:28.679 --> 00:04:30.858
And this may evolve to something else.

00:04:30.858 --> 00:04:33.876
I'm not sold on being a Youtuber
for the rest of my life.

00:04:33.876 --> 00:04:36.000
Something will change, I'll shift

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.244
and I'll go off and do something else.

00:04:37.244 --> 00:04:38.857
It'll still be likely around
helping entrepreneurs,

00:04:38.857 --> 00:04:39.940
that's my passion.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.827
But how to do it will
shift, will evolve and grow.

00:04:42.827 --> 00:04:45.070
My introductions on these
channels are changing.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.573
The video series that I try.

00:04:46.573 --> 00:04:48.382
So it's like there's the macro changes

00:04:48.382 --> 00:04:49.713
of the projects I take on,

00:04:49.713 --> 00:04:52.124
from speaking to website to Youtube.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.295
And then there's a micro evolution inside.

00:04:54.295 --> 00:04:56.364
From launching a new series,
and testing and seeing

00:04:56.364 --> 00:04:58.271
and always trying new things to see

00:04:58.271 --> 00:05:00.115
how it can improve and make it better.

00:05:00.115 --> 00:05:03.698
If I stop doing those
things, I would start to die.

00:05:03.698 --> 00:05:06.027
And then I'd have to get out of it.

00:05:06.027 --> 00:05:08.187
So stop dying in your business.

00:05:08.187 --> 00:05:11.927
Continue, constantly,
to introduce new things,

00:05:11.927 --> 00:05:15.525
to get this thing excited and invigorated

00:05:15.525 --> 00:05:17.498
so you never get bored with your business.

00:05:17.498 --> 00:05:20.648
So the question today is I'm curious,

00:05:20.648 --> 00:05:23.547
have you ever been bored in your company

00:05:23.547 --> 00:05:25.756
and what did you do to change it?

00:05:25.756 --> 00:05:26.955
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:26.955 --> 00:05:28.047
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:28.047 --> 00:05:30.291
I also want to give a quick
shout out to C.X. Koehler,

00:05:30.291 --> 00:05:32.584
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:05:32.584 --> 00:05:34.543
I understand it was as a gift actually.

00:05:34.543 --> 00:05:36.492
So I hope you enjoy the gift

00:05:36.492 --> 00:05:38.473
and you're reading it and
applying it to your life

00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:39.919
and your business.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:41.236
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:41.236 --> 00:05:42.640
I believe in you.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.681
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:44.681 --> 00:05:46.693
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:46.693 --> 00:05:49.478
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:49.478 --> 00:05:52.302
for another shot of entspresso.

00:05:52.302 --> 00:05:54.904
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:54.904 --> 00:05:59.071
♫ Entspresso keep me going ♫

00:06:01.346 --> 00:06:04.232
- The Lion King was of
course, it was huge.

00:06:04.232 --> 00:06:06.841
Especially 'cause I did it
for all the wrong reasons.

00:06:06.841 --> 00:06:09.178
I mean I did it for my daughter because

00:06:09.178 --> 00:06:11.217
I wanted to show off as dad.

00:06:11.217 --> 00:06:13.555
And I was doing all these grown up movies

00:06:13.555 --> 00:06:14.884
where people were getting killed

00:06:14.884 --> 00:06:17.086
and I couldn't take her to a premier.

00:06:17.086 --> 00:06:21.253
I wanted to do something to
take my kid to a premier.

00:06:23.855 --> 00:06:27.057
And it was surprisingly
emotional doing that movie.

00:06:27.057 --> 00:06:29.640
It deals with a father's death.

00:06:32.679 --> 00:06:34.762
It's got a lot more depth

00:06:35.899 --> 00:06:37.811
than the surface that we believe.

00:06:37.811 --> 00:06:40.434
And it shocked me, my own response.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:42.210
You know once I started writing on it,

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:46.293
because I was thinking, oh
this is going to be easy.

00:06:48.303 --> 00:06:50.453
And it wasn't like it was hard.

00:06:50.453 --> 00:06:54.620
But the emotional involvements
only became profound

00:06:56.109 --> 00:06:57.776
as supposed to hard.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.080
And really with Lion King,

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.757
that got Terry Malick
interested in me for instance.

00:07:05.757 --> 00:07:09.141
Terry loved Lion King and
wanted me to do Thin Man Lines.

00:07:09.141 --> 00:07:12.683
So all these things,
working with Ridley Scott.

00:07:12.683 --> 00:07:17.278
I mean we've done some
really good movies together.

00:07:17.278 --> 00:07:19.272
And they're stylistically so different.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.712
I mean Black Rain is so
different from Thelma and Louise.

00:07:21.712 --> 00:07:23.746
It's so different from Gladiators,

00:07:23.746 --> 00:07:24.871
it's so different from Hannibal,

00:07:24.871 --> 00:07:26.975
it's so different from Black Hunt Down.

00:07:26.975 --> 00:07:28.404
It's so different from Match stick men.

00:07:28.404 --> 00:07:30.904
I'm sure I'm leaving some out.

00:07:32.982 --> 00:07:35.982
So working with people who, like me,

00:07:37.799 --> 00:07:40.122
they get a little bored
doing the same thing

00:07:40.122 --> 00:07:44.289
and off they go trying to do
something completely different.

00:07:45.239 --> 00:07:47.989
I mean that's the big part of it.

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:53.482
- Reality television shows is so big now.

00:07:53.482 --> 00:07:57.333
I like to get on the bandwagon,
whenever I can find one.

00:07:57.333 --> 00:08:00.456
And I felt if we're going to do a cartoon

00:08:00.456 --> 00:08:03.240
an animated movie for the Hub Network,

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.242
I want to make it more
different than anything before.

00:08:06.242 --> 00:08:09.639
Why not make it a
reality animated cartoon.

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:12.141
So in order to make it a reality cartoon,

00:08:12.141 --> 00:08:13.683
we have real people in it.

00:08:13.683 --> 00:08:16.252
I'm as real as I know I can get.

00:08:16.252 --> 00:08:18.416
So I'm in it, we have a
few other real people in.

00:08:18.416 --> 00:08:19.858
- [Larry King] You got
Jim Belushi isn't it?

00:08:19.858 --> 00:08:20.753
- Jim Belushi.

00:08:20.753 --> 00:08:22.119
- [Larry King] Christian Slater?

00:08:22.119 --> 00:08:23.325
- They're doing the voices.

00:08:23.325 --> 00:08:26.837
- Teri Hatcher, Sean Astin,
Armie Hammer is in it.

00:08:26.837 --> 00:08:29.283
Flee and Darren Chris, they're
all voicing superheroes.

00:08:29.283 --> 00:08:31.234
Are the superheroes new heroes?

00:08:31.234 --> 00:08:32.674
- They're all new heroes.

00:08:32.674 --> 00:08:36.012
Actually they're aliens
from another planet.

00:08:36.012 --> 00:08:39.055
Which is not unusual in a superhero story.

00:08:39.055 --> 00:08:40.968
- Let me tell you, in order
to have something different,

00:08:40.968 --> 00:08:42.946
you are going to have to
do something different.

00:08:42.946 --> 00:08:44.225
In order to have something more,

00:08:44.225 --> 00:08:46.303
you have to do something
you haven't done yet.

00:08:46.303 --> 00:08:48.234
I had to say the things
I didn't want to say,

00:08:48.234 --> 00:08:49.865
do the things I didn't feel like doing

00:08:49.865 --> 00:08:53.282
to have the life I knew I wanted, period.

00:08:54.236 --> 00:08:55.425
Period.

00:08:55.425 --> 00:08:57.284
And all I did was give instructions.

00:08:57.284 --> 00:09:00.343
Here, do this bit size, do this
bite size, do this bite size

00:09:00.343 --> 00:09:04.662
bite size, digestible, palatable
pieces of what you can do.

00:09:04.662 --> 00:09:06.618
Does that sound good you guys?

00:09:06.618 --> 00:09:07.451
And when you look up,

00:09:07.451 --> 00:09:09.700
and you don't have to
have a magnificent change

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.299
over 12 months, have a
small change over 30 days.

00:09:12.299 --> 00:09:13.859
And a small change over 30 days.

00:09:13.859 --> 00:09:16.903
Your break through will
come in needle point moves.

00:09:16.903 --> 00:09:18.502
And you'll look up in five years,

00:09:18.502 --> 00:09:20.688
and not recognize your life.

